---
source: tests/contract_snapshots.rs
expression: help
---
$ robostickies --help
Small repository-local notes for humans and agents, through CLI and MCP

Usage: robostickies [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init       Scaffold .robostickies without overwriting existing notes or tags
  add        Record nonempty UTF-8 text. Markdown or plain text is preferred
  get        Read a note by its full UUID
  update     Edit selected note fields; unmentioned fields remain unchanged
  archive    Archive a resolved or obsolete note
  unarchive  Restore an archived note to active status
  list       Browse notes with optional filters
  search     Search note bodies for a case-insensitive literal substring
  review     Produce complete review material; visibility defaults to public
  tags       Define tags for labeling notes, with optional descriptions and guidance
  publish    Copy a private note into public storage, retaining the original
  context    Read session guidance, tag names and optional descriptions, startup details, and an AGENTS.md snippet
  config     Inspect effective configuration and its source files
  doctor     Validate source files and Git privacy protections
  reindex    Rebuild the disposable redb index from Markdown sources
  upgrade    Upgrade the shared store data version, preserving notes and guidance
  mcp        Serve MCP over stdio; stdout is exclusively protocol data
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --repo <REPO>                Directory override; defaults to the Git root containing the startup CWD, or that CWD outside Git
      --json                       Emit structured JSON instead of human-readable output
      --user-config <USER_CONFIG>  Override the platform-standard user configuration file
      --no-user-config             Disable user configuration for reproducible automation
  -h, --help                       Print help
  -V, --version                    Print version

$ robostickies add --help
Record nonempty UTF-8 text. Markdown or plain text is preferred

Usage: robostickies add [OPTIONS] [BODY]

Arguments:
  [BODY]  UTF-8 text, or - to read stdin. Use Markdown for tag guidance

Options:
      --file <FILE>                Read UTF-8 text from a file, or - for stdin
      --repo <REPO>                Directory override; defaults to the Git root containing the startup CWD, or that CWD outside Git
      --body-format <BODY_FORMAT>  Advisory body hint: markdown, text, yaml, or another nonblank string
      --json                       Emit structured JSON instead of human-readable output
      --tag <TAGS>                 Defined tag name, e.g. fresh-install; repeat for multiple tags
      --user-config <USER_CONFIG>  Override the platform-standard user configuration file
      --no-user-config             Disable user configuration for reproducible automation
      --private                    Keep the new tag or note in ignored private storage
      --public                     Select public creation; private note tags still require private storage
  -h, --help                       Print help

$ robostickies update --help
Edit selected note fields; unmentioned fields remain unchanged

Usage: robostickies update [OPTIONS] --if-match <IF_MATCH> <ID> [BODY]

Arguments:
  <ID>
  [BODY]  UTF-8 text, or - to read stdin. Use Markdown for tag guidance

Options:
      --file <FILE>                Read UTF-8 text from a file, or - for stdin
      --repo <REPO>                Directory override; defaults to the Git root containing the startup CWD, or that CWD outside Git
      --body-format <BODY_FORMAT>  Set an advisory body hint; omitted hints remain unchanged
      --json                       Emit structured JSON instead of human-readable output
      --clear-body-format          Remove an existing string body hint
      --user-config <USER_CONFIG>  Override the platform-standard user configuration file
      --no-user-config             Disable user configuration for reproducible automation
      --tag <TAGS>                 Replace all tags with this set; repeat the flag for multiple tags
      --clear-tags
      --status <STATUS>            [possible values: active, archived]
      --private                    Keep the new tag or note in ignored private storage
      --public                     Select public creation; private note tags still require private storage
      --if-match <IF_MATCH>        Required last-read revision; re-read and reconcile after a conflict
  -h, --help                       Print help

$ robostickies tags --help
Define tags for labeling notes, with optional descriptions and guidance

Usage: robostickies tags [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  create  Define a tag name, with an optional description and usage guidance
  list    List tag names and any descriptions
  get     Read a tag's optional description and usage guidance
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --repo <REPO>                Directory override; defaults to the Git root containing the startup CWD, or that CWD outside Git
      --json                       Emit structured JSON instead of human-readable output
      --user-config <USER_CONFIG>  Override the platform-standard user configuration file
      --no-user-config             Disable user configuration for reproducible automation
  -h, --help                       Print help

Tag fields:
  NAME           Required tag name used with --tag, e.g. fresh-install.
  --description  Optional short explanation shown by tags list.
  BODY           Optional Markdown guidance on when and how to use the tag.

Examples:
  robostickies tags create fresh-install
  robostickies tags create onboarding --description "Setup and first-run checks" \
    "Record setup steps, missing tools, and first-run errors."
  robostickies add "Setup required an extra PATH entry" --tag fresh-install

Self-explanatory tags usually do not need a description.
Use tags get onboarding to read the description and guidance.
Name-only creation in a legacy store requires an explicit robostickies upgrade.

$ robostickies tags create --help
Define a tag name, with an optional description and usage guidance

Usage: robostickies tags create [OPTIONS] <NAME> [BODY]

Arguments:
  <NAME>  Tag name used by --tag, e.g. fresh-install
  [BODY]  UTF-8 text, or - to read stdin. Use Markdown for tag guidance

Options:
      --description <DESCRIPTION>  Optional catalog explanation; self-explanatory tags usually need none
      --repo <REPO>                Directory override; defaults to the Git root containing the startup CWD, or that CWD outside Git
      --file <FILE>                Read UTF-8 text from a file, or - for stdin
      --json                       Emit structured JSON instead of human-readable output
      --read-on-start
      --user-config <USER_CONFIG>  Override the platform-standard user configuration file
      --no-user-config             Disable user configuration for reproducible automation
      --private                    Keep the new tag or note in ignored private storage
      --public                     Select public creation; private note tags still require private storage
  -h, --help                       Print help

Tag fields:
  NAME           Required tag name used with --tag, e.g. fresh-install.
  --description  Optional short explanation shown by tags list.
  BODY           Optional Markdown guidance on when and how to use the tag.

Examples:
  robostickies tags create fresh-install
  robostickies tags create onboarding --description "Setup and first-run checks" \
    "Record setup steps, missing tools, and first-run errors."
  robostickies add "Setup required an extra PATH entry" --tag fresh-install

Self-explanatory tags usually do not need a description.
Use tags get onboarding to read the description and guidance.
Name-only creation in a legacy store requires an explicit robostickies upgrade.

$ robostickies publish --help
Copy a private note into public storage, retaining the original

Usage: robostickies publish [OPTIONS] --if-match <IF_MATCH> <ID> [BODY]

Arguments:
  <ID>
  [BODY]  UTF-8 text, or - to read stdin. Use Markdown for tag guidance

Options:
      --dry-run
      --repo <REPO>                Directory override; defaults to the Git root containing the startup CWD, or that CWD outside Git
      --file <FILE>                Read UTF-8 text from a file, or - for stdin
      --json                       Emit structured JSON instead of human-readable output
      --body-format <BODY_FORMAT>  Set a public hint explicitly; the private source hint is never copied
      --user-config <USER_CONFIG>  Override the platform-standard user configuration file
      --no-user-config             Disable user configuration for reproducible automation
      --tag <TAGS>                 Replace the public tag set; private tags are forbidden
      --clear-tags
      --if-match <IF_MATCH>        Required source revision, including for --dry-run
  -h, --help                       Print help

$ robostickies upgrade --help
Upgrade the shared store data version, preserving notes and guidance

Usage: robostickies upgrade [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --dry-run                    Validate and preview the migration without changing source files
      --repo <REPO>                Directory override; defaults to the Git root containing the startup CWD, or that CWD outside Git
      --defer                      Decline this optional target until the recommended target changes
      --json                       Emit structured JSON instead of human-readable output
      --keep-snapshot              Retain the private recovery snapshot after a successful upgrade
      --user-config <USER_CONFIG>  Override the platform-standard user configuration file
      --no-user-config             Disable user configuration for reproducible automation
  -h, --help                       Print help

$ robostickies mcp --help
Serve MCP over stdio; stdout is exclusively protocol data.

Existing servers keep their compiled build after installation. Restart or reconnect the client, then call the MCP version tool to identify that server.

Usage: robostickies mcp [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --repo <REPO>
          Directory override; defaults to the Git root containing the startup CWD, or that CWD outside Git

      --json
          Emit structured JSON instead of human-readable output

      --user-config <USER_CONFIG>
          Override the platform-standard user configuration file

      --no-user-config
          Disable user configuration for reproducible automation

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
